  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Crisp fall weather through the week with cool \ntemperatures. \n\nHigh pressure will remain over the region through at least the\nnext week, with broad 500 mb troughing over much of the \nsouthern and eastern U.S. Breezy northerly winds today will \naffect Southside VA as well as the NC Piedmont. With good \nradiational cooling conditions most nights, overnight lows will \nbe in the 30s and 40s areawide. Our mountain zones froze last \nnight, so we are not including frost in the weather grids, or \nissuing anymore Frost or Freeze headlines, although it may be \npossible. Some river valley fog is expected most nights. The \ngrowing season remains open for the Piedmont and Roanoke Valley \nat this time.\n\nWinds vary slightly from the northwest to the northwest by\nThursday, and surface high pressure will continue to provide \ndry and clear weather. Temperatures will gradually moderate \ntowards seasonal normals, with high temperatures in the 60s and \n70s.",
